QcRilAm: per-slot AIDL response, wait for the HAL, recover from RIL and audioserver restarts

Project: packages/apps/QcRilAm (TrebleDroid, branch android-16.0)

The AIDL path kept one response interface in a file-level variable. On a device whose vendor
serves IQcRilAudio/slot1 and /slot2 the second registration overwrote it, so every response
for slot 1 was sent to the RIL process of slot 2. The service was also looked up once at boot
without waiting and never again: a RIL process that registered late or restarted left the
phone without the audio parameters of voice calls until the next reboot. The vendor client
this app replaces (com.qualcomm.qti.telephonyservice) keeps the response per slot, waits for
the declared service, re-registers from a death recipient and reports audioserver death and
recovery through IQcRilAudio.setError; this change does the same.

- one connection object per slot with its own response interface and lock
- ServiceManager.waitForDeclaredService on a per-slot thread, retry on failure
- linkToDeath and re-registration
- AudioManager.setAudioServerStateCallback -> setError(STATUS_SERVER_DIED / STATUS_OK)
- answer the RIL instead of blocking in AudioManager while audioserver is down

The HIDL paths are unchanged.

Revision 2 (2026-10-10, after the first DSU boot): the registration is logged step by step
and a warning is logged when setRequestInterface has not returned after 10 s. On that boot
both slot threads found the HAL and then never reported success or failure.

